# Local verification artifacts only - never a fixture. Mirrors the sibling
# live/e2e/estate/.gitignore (singular), which has carried these three rules
# since P0.2 for the same reason: a stray run here must not leave a provider
# cache or a state file in the next person's `git status`. This directory
# never had one, so 31 .terraform/ directories accumulated (issue #1333).
#
# Scoped here rather than at the repo root deliberately. 53 tracked files
# live inside .terraform/ directories under internal/ - happypath's
# modules.json and the internal/command/testdata/backend-* fixtures - where
# the directory's CONTENTS are what the test asserts on. A root-level
# .terraform/ rule would not untrack those, but it would make the next
# fixture added there invisible to whoever adds it.
.terraform/
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup
